## Write an equation from each pattern
Pattern 1 has 1 cross, so $T_1 = 1$. Pattern 2 has 3 crosses, so $T_2 = 3$.
\frac{1}{2} + b + c &= 1
b + c &= \frac{1}{2}
2 + 2b + c &= 3
2b + c &= 1
## Subtract the equations to find b
(2b + c) - (b + c) &= 1 - \frac{1}{2}
b &= \frac{1}{2}
## Substitute b to find c
\frac{1}{2} + c &= \frac{1}{2}
c &= 0
ANSWER: b = \frac{1}{2}, \quad c = 0

## Convert the volume to litres
\text{Litres} &= 1\,000\,000 \times 1000
&= 10^9
## Divide by the flow rate to find the time in seconds
\text{Time} &= \frac{10^9}{250\,000}
&= 4000 \text{ seconds}
## Convert to minutes
\text{Time} &= \frac{4000}{60}
&\approx 66.67 \text{ minutes}
&\approx 67 \text{ minutes}
ANSWER: 67 \text{ minutes}

## Find the distance of one circuit
C &= 2\pi r
&= 2\pi(0.5)
&= \pi \text{ km}
## Find the distance of 3 circuits
D &= 3\pi
&\approx 9.42 \text{ km}
## Divide by the speed to find the time
T &= \frac{D}{S}
T &= \frac{3\pi}{6}
&= \frac{\pi}{2} \text{ hours}
&\approx 1.5708 \text{ hours}
## Convert to minutes
\text{Time} &= \frac{\pi}{2} \times 60
&= 30\pi
&\approx 94.25 \text{ minutes}
&\approx 94 \text{ minutes}
ANSWER: 94 \text{ minutes}

## Find her distance on day 5
Each day she walks 1.15 times the day before. Day 5 is four increases after day 1.
\text{Distance} &= 3(1.15)^4
&\approx 5.2470 \text{ km}
## Divide by her speed to find the time
T &= \frac{D}{S}
T &= \frac{3(1.15)^4}{4}
&\approx 1.3118 \text{ hours}
## Convert to minutes
\text{Time} &= 1.3118 \times 60
&\approx 78.7 \text{ minutes}
&\approx 79 \text{ minutes}
ANSWER: 79 \text{ minutes}

## Find their combined speed
They walk in opposite directions, so together they cover one full circuit before meeting again.
\text{Combined speed} &= 6 + 4
&= 10 \text{ km/h}
## Find the time until they meet
T &= \frac{D}{S}
T &= \frac{\pi}{10}
&\approx 0.314 \text{ hours}
## Find how far John walks in that time
D &= 6 \times \frac{\pi}{10}
&= \frac{3\pi}{5} \text{ km}
&\approx 1.885 \text{ km}
## Convert to metres
D &= 1.885 \times 1000
&= 1885 \text{ m}
ANSWER: 1885 \text{ m}

## Count the outcomes with left foot
Left foot goes with each of the 4 colours, so 4 outcomes out of 16.
## Write the probability
P(\text{left foot}) &= \frac{4}{16}
&= \frac{1}{4}
ANSWER: \frac{1}{4}

## Find each probability from the colour spinner
P(\text{red}) &= \frac{1}{4}
P(\text{yellow}) &= \frac{1}{4}
## Add, since red and yellow cannot both happen
P(\text{red or yellow}) &= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{4}
&= \frac{2}{4}
&= \frac{1}{2}
ANSWER: \frac{1}{2}

## Find each probability
P(\text{right hand}) &= \frac{1}{4}
P(\text{blue}) &= \frac{1}{4}
## Multiply, since "and" with separate spinners means multiply
P(\text{right hand and blue}) &= \frac{1}{4} \times \frac{1}{4}
&= \frac{1}{16}
ANSWER: \frac{1}{16}

## Use the rule for "or"
P(\text{RH or blue}) &= P(\text{RH}) + P(\text{blue}) - P(\text{RH and blue})
We subtract the overlap, because right hand and blue is counted in both.
## Substitute and work out
P(\text{RH or blue}) &= \frac{1}{4} + \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{16}
&= \frac{4}{16} + \frac{4}{16} - \frac{1}{16}
&= \frac{7}{16}
ANSWER: \frac{7}{16}

## Find the radius as the distance from C to A
r &= \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
r &= \sqrt{(6 - 2)^2 + (2 - (-1))^2}
&= \sqrt{4^2 + 3^2}
&= \sqrt{16 + 9}
&= \sqrt{25}
&= 5
## Write the equation using centre (2, -1) and radius 5
(x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 &= r^2
(x - 2)^2 + (y - (-1))^2 &= 5^2
(x - 2)^2 + (y + 1)^2 &= 25
ANSWER: r = 5,\ (x - 2)^2 + (y + 1)^2 = 25
